  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Round the zone – four one-touch passes and a shot",
  "description": "Four lines and a goalkeeper in one half: A and D in the corners by the goal, B and C along the boards out at the defender positions. A passes down to B and runs in a curve into the slot. The ball then goes round the zone with one-touch passes: B to C, C to D and D in to A, who shoots first time.\n\nRotation: A goes to B, B to C, C to D and D to A. Also run it mirrored, so that A starts from the other corner. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball – then the passer can play it first time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Passes hard, along the floor and on target."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: time the run so that you reach the slot as D gets the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time and hit the target."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "main",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "focus": [
